Package: spax
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Accessibility and Allocation Modeling
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Songyos", "Rajborirug", , "songyos.r@psu.ac.th", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5000-7409"))
Description: Spatial accessibility analysis using floating catchment area (FCA)
    methods and experimental static conditional-logit allocation models with an
    outside option.
    FCA functions produce accessibility surfaces for independent supply indicators.
    The allocation workflow provides checked numeric preparation, observation-based
    calibration, requested-location prediction and fixed-parameter supply scenarios.
    Saved results retain input declarations, support information and fit diagnostics.
    A conditional facility-case bootstrap is available for static allocation
    models with a fitted outside mass and a decay kernel that is smooth in sigma,
    built in or declared, with an optional fitted supply elasticity beta, and an
    explicitly declared observation process. Its coverage was evaluated for
    Gaussian decay with fitted sigma and v0; other kernels and a fitted beta use
    the same procedure without a separate coverage study.
